From: Benjamin Otte <otte@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] x11: use the device display for tool property atoms

An X11 display can be open while the default display is Wayland. Using
the default atom converter on an XI2 property event then treats a
GdkWaylandDisplay as GdkX11Display and crashes in g_hash_table_lookup().

Backport the XI2 change from GTK 4 without removing the GTK 3 public API.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/commit/920259c25070986b13675fd86f3def1b805dc00d
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
--- a/gdk/x11/gdkdevicemanager-xi2.c
+++ b/gdk/x11/gdkdevicemanager-xi2.c
@@ -1194,7 +1194,8 @@
                                 GUINT_TO_POINTER (ev->deviceid));
 
   if (device != NULL &&
-      ev->property == gdk_x11_get_xatom_by_name ("Wacom Serial IDs"))
+      ev->property == gdk_x11_get_xatom_by_name_for_display (gdk_device_get_display (device),
+                                                          "Wacom Serial IDs"))
     {
       GdkDeviceTool *tool = NULL;
       guint serial_id = 0, tool_id = 0;
